{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785251755,"nonce":"JwykfrYiWEYOh1gh/4e1H5j0PTA=","message":"**DECIDED (architect, 2026-07-28): option (a) — ADR-0061 part 4 stands verbatim, and the cold upload stays on the critical path to `Succeeded`.**\n\nRecorded in ADR-0062 part 3, in place, next to the \"no network in the path\" sentence that invited the confusion. The claim that moved is that one: it was true of the **fold** and false of the **Attempt**.\n\nThe reasoning, so it is not re-litigated later. What now gets uploaded is only the **change set**, whereas today's drain ships the *entire* workspace over the `exec` tar tunnel whether it changed or not. So an Export that folds locally and then uploads what the Step actually wrote moves **strictly less** than the status quo while keeping a durability guarantee the status quo also has. Option (b) would have traded a real correctness property for a speedup mostly already banked elsewhere.\n\nAgainst the acceptance criteria:\n\n- [x] A decision, recorded in ADR-0062: what must be durable before `Succeeded`, and where it lives — the snapshot, in **cold**, before the Attempt may reach `Succeeded`.\n- [x] The cold upload's cost is stated in the ADR rather than discovered in a benchmark — one upload per Step, sized by the change set, on the critical path.\n- [x] ADR-0061 part 4 holds **verbatim**; no amendment needed, and the ADR now says so explicitly rather than leaving it inferable.\n- [ ] **A node or service dying immediately after a Step exits 0 cannot leave a `Succeeded` Attempt whose evidence is gone** — this is the one criterion the decision alone does not satisfy. It needs the ordering *enforced in code*: the cold upload must complete before the Attempt is reported settled. That lands with the wiring slice (`ce91801`), not here, and it is the criterion to test rather than assume.\n\nTwo consequences carried into the ADR. The upload cannot be skipped for content cold already holds without an existence primitive on the `ObjectStore` port (a separate filed gap), so the first implementation pays for content cold may already have. And the laziness this ADR buys is on the **read** side — the write side is bounded by the change set, which is what part 5 exists for.\n\nLeaving this open on the last criterion only.","files":null}]}